Task 3.3 – Implement the Screen 
Java Swing Implementation
The following program implements the Campus Library Search Screen using JFrame, JPanel, BorderLayout, FlowLayout, JTextField, JComboBox, JButton and JTextArea.

Program: LibrarySearchWindow.java

import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;
import java.awt.event.*;

public class LibrarySearchWindow extends JFrame {

    JTextField searchField;
    JComboBox<String> categoryChoice;
    JButton searchButton, prevButton, nextButton, reserveButton;
    JTextArea resultsArea;
    JLabel statusLabel;

    int currentPage = 1;

    public LibrarySearchWindow() {

        setTitle("Campus Library Search");
        setSize(800, 500);
        setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);

        // Main layout
        setLayout(new BorderLayout(5, 5));

        // 1. Title Panel
        JPanel titlePanel = new JPanel(new FlowLayout(FlowLayout.CENTER));

        JLabel title = new JLabel("CAMPUS LIBRARY SEARCH");
        title.setFont(new Font("Arial", Font.BOLD, 22));

        titlePanel.add(title);

        add(titlePanel, BorderLayout.NORTH);

        // 2. Search Panel
        JPanel searchPanel = new JPanel(new FlowLayout(FlowLayout.LEFT));

        searchField = new JTextField(25);

        String[] categories = {
            "All Categories",
            "Computer Science",
            "Mathematics",
            "Electronics",
            "Physics"
        };

        categoryChoice = new JComboBox<>(categories);
        searchButton = new JButton("Search");

        searchPanel.add(new JLabel("Search:"));
        searchPanel.add(searchField);
        searchPanel.add(categoryChoice);
        searchPanel.add(searchButton);

        // 3. Results Panel
        JPanel resultsPanel = new JPanel(new BorderLayout());

        resultsArea = new JTextArea();
        resultsArea.setEditable(false);
        resultsArea.setFont(new Font("Arial", Font.PLAIN, 15));

        JScrollPane scrollPane = new JScrollPane(resultsArea);

        resultsPanel.add(scrollPane, BorderLayout.CENTER);

        // Search and results container
        JPanel centerPanel = new JPanel(new BorderLayout());

        centerPanel.add(searchPanel, BorderLayout.NORTH);
        centerPanel.add(resultsPanel, BorderLayout.CENTER);

        add(centerPanel, BorderLayout.CENTER);

        // 4. Navigation Panel
        JPanel navigationPanel = new JPanel(new FlowLayout());

        prevButton = new JButton("Prev");
        nextButton = new JButton("Next");
        reserveButton = new JButton("Reserve");

        navigationPanel.add(prevButton);
        navigationPanel.add(nextButton);
        navigationPanel.add(reserveButton);

        // 5. Status Panel
        JPanel statusPanel = new JPanel(new FlowLayout(FlowLayout.LEFT));

        statusLabel = new JLabel("Status: Ready");
        statusPanel.add(statusLabel);

        // Bottom container
        JPanel bottomPanel = new JPanel(new BorderLayout());

        bottomPanel.add(navigationPanel, BorderLayout.CENTER);
        bottomPanel.add(statusPanel, BorderLayout.SOUTH);

        add(bottomPanel, BorderLayout.SOUTH);

        // Event handling

        searchButton.addActionListener(e -> searchBooks());

        searchField.addActionListener(e -> searchBooks());

        prevButton.addActionListener(e -> {
            if (currentPage > 1) {
                currentPage--;
                statusLabel.setText("Status: Previous page " + currentPage);
            }
        });

        nextButton.addActionListener(e -> {
            currentPage++;
            statusLabel.setText("Status: Next page " + currentPage);
        });

        reserveButton.addActionListener(e -> {
            if (resultsArea.getSelectedText() != null) {
                statusLabel.setText("Status: Reservation requested");
            } else {
                statusLabel.setText("Status: Select a book first");
            }
        });

        setLocationRelativeTo(null);
        setVisible(true);
    }

    private void searchBooks() {

        String keyword = searchField.getText().trim();
        String category = (String) categoryChoice.getSelectedItem();

        if (keyword.isEmpty()) {
            statusLabel.setText("Status: Enter a book name");
            return;
        }

        resultsArea.setText(
            "Search Results\n\n" +
            "Book 1: " + keyword + " - " + category + "\n" +
            "Book 2: Introduction to " + keyword + "\n" +
            "Book 3: Advanced " + keyword + "\n"
        );

        currentPage = 1;
        statusLabel.setText("Status: Search completed");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> {
            new LibrarySearchWindow();
        });
    }
}



Explanation of the Implementation
Component	Implementation
JFrame	Creates the main library search window.
Title JPanel	Displays the application title.
JTextField	Accepts the book name or keyword.
JComboBox	Allows selection of a book category.
Search JButton	Initiates the search operation.
JTextArea	Displays the search results.
JScrollPane	Provides scrolling for large result lists.
Prev JButton	Moves to the previous page.
Next JButton	Moves to the next page.
Reserve JButton	Handles a reservation request.
JLabel	Displays the current status.

How resizing works:
- The main JFrame uses BorderLayout.
- The title stays in the North region.
- The search row stays above the results.
- The results area occupies the Center region and expands when the window grows.
- The navigation buttons and status message stay in the South region.
- FlowLayout maintains the preferred sizes of the controls instead of stretching them to fill the available width.
Note: This is a working GUI demonstration with sample search results. Actual library database searching, pagination and reservation processing would require database integration.
